{
    "description": "load_plan rejects a streamline commissionable_depth below the number of declared levels. Mirrors Go's depth_less_than_levels (internal/config/rules.go:969). HEU-612. Unlike its two sibling fixtures this one mutates two fields of the calculate_streamline base plan, and both are needed: the base declares one level at depth 5, so dropping depth alone gives 1 >= 1 and passes. The table grows to two levels first, then depth drops to 1. This plan is a hand-maintained copy of the one embedded in calculate_streamline.json's setup_raw, mutated as described. Nothing keeps them in sync: if that base plan's shape changes, this file keeps passing because the plan stops deserializing rather than because the rule fired. Change one, change all. HEU-604 tracks consolidating the copies.",
